PayUSER util V1.01ß by Zwinx/RAGE
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
This neat little util is written to be used with /X 2.xx and 3.xx. It's easy
to use and install.

FEATURES
~~~~~~~~
× This little util keeps track of your payusers, and other time-limited
  disabled-users.
× Easy to use, built in PayUser-editor, wich is scanning directly from
  your user.data. When searching for users, you can use wildcards (like
  the built in User-Editor, or like the wildcard sequence during logon).
× You don't have to mind >AT ALL< about the disabled users. When their
  time comes, their disabled ratio returns EXACTLY to normal. Downloaded
  bytes during this time WILL NOT be counted or added to the users account.

INSTALLATION NOTICE
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
IF YOU USE /X VERSION 2.x THEN YOU CAN'T USE THE SUPPLIED SCRIPTFILE TO
INSTALL/UPDATE THIS DOOR!
YOU MUST FOLLOW THE INSTRUCTIONS EXACTLY DURING THE INSTALLATION, OTHER-
WISE THE DOOR WILL NOT WORK!
YOU MUST HAVE USER.DATA IN BBS:

/X 2.x INSTALLATION
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
× Make a directory called "PayUser" in DOORS: and one directory called
  "Payers" in DOORS:PayUser

ex.
HD:> makedir DOORS:PayUser
HD:> makedir DOORS:PayUser/Payers

× Unpack the Space.LHA archive in DOORS:Space.

ex.
HD:> cd DOORS:PayUser
HD:BBS/DOORS/PayUser> lha x RAM:RG-PAYUS.lha

× Insert the following line in your BBS.CMD file. Read /X documentation for
  further information.

---CUT---
PAY       RM010DOORS:Space/Space.rexx
---CUT---

× Edit BBS:<conf>/DownLoadMsg.txt. Remember to edit all conferences!

ex.
---CUT---
~
~CC_PAY

Go on an' download! But don't forget the "u" key!
---CUT---

/X 3.x INSTALLATION
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
× Unpack the RG-PAYUS.LHA archive to RAM:
 
ex.
HD:> cd RAM:
Ram Disk:> lha x RAM:RG-PAYUS.lha

× Execute the AE3.x_Install-script.

ex.
Ram Disk:> AE3.x_Install

HOW TO USE
~~~~~~~~~~
Let's make an example: WarezMan have paied you for disabled for two months.
To start with, enter the door by typing "PAY" (In fact, you CAN also enter
the door by typing "D").

ex.
---
DaGcEnTRaL 9o²1o [3:[%] MaIN ZooNE [%]] Menu (99998 mins. left): PAY

---
If you are the sysop you will get the following screen:
---
PayUSER Version 1.01 - Written by Zwinx/Rage!
                                             
Do you wish to edit stats (y/N)? 
---
Type "Y" here, everything else will exit the door.

You will now be asked for the username to edit. Wildcards are allowed.

ex.
UserName: Warez*

Expand: WarezMan Correct (Y/n)? 
---

When you have choosen the correct user, the mainscreen will appear.

ex.
---
PayUSER Version 1.01 - Written by Zwinx/Rage!

PAY-INACTIVE     UserName: WAREZMAN
               Start Date: NOT STARTED
         Month(s) Payment: 1

       Original downloads: 220
       Original downbytes: 34442524

Edit [P]ayment, [C]lear Start Date, [R]emove payuser or E[x]it?
---
"PAY-INACTIVE" means that this user has no previous Pay-User Account.
If a user has a previous account, the text would say "PAY-ACTIVE".
"Start Date" is a combined field for StartDate of disabled "session" and
status. There are 2 valid statuses (? spelling?) and they are: NOT STARTED
and REMOVED. NOT STARTED means that this user have never used his PayUser
accont. When he uses it for the first time, this field will be changed to
the date of the first download.
ex.
Start Date: 19940201
            ^   ^ ^
            |   | |
            |   | +- Day
            |   +--- Month
            +------- Year

The other possible status in this field is "REMOVED". It will be explained
later.

The P-command.
Default settings are one month disabled. This is easily changed by typing
"P" and enter a new number of months. This can be changed on a user with
Status "NOT STARTED" as well as a user wich has already started he's
disabled session. You CAN change it on users with status "REMOVED" as well,
but it's rather pointless.
The C-command.
This command is used when you for any reason want to reset the disabled
time for a user. The "status" will be changed to "NOT STARTED".
The R-command.
This command is used for removing the PayUser Account for a user. The
status will be changed to "REMOVED". NOTE: The user will be "PAY-ACTIVE"
and will have DISABLED until he tries to download next time. When he
does, he will be informed that the PayUser Account is removed. He's normal
Ratio, Downloaded bytes and Downloaded files will be resetted to Normal.

OTHER NOTES
~~~~~~~~~~~
When a user with a never-used Pay Account downloads for the first time, the
ratio is changed to "DISABLED" and the downloaded bytes and files are
changed to zero. Everything will b back to normal when the Disabled time
is over.
It's really easy to use this door! Try it out!

